THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL THAT IS CITED BUT NOT INCLUDED
---------------------------------------------------
The documentation (Romenagri/TRANSLITERATION.md, section 12) cites, as
sources of facts, five public web pages: Apple's DEVANAGA.TXT mapping table,
the ICU converter source ucnvisci.cpp, and the Wikipedia article on ISCII (for
byte values); and a copy of the Unicode Character Database file
CompositionExclusions.txt and a thread of the Unicode mailing list on
composition exclusions for Devanagari (for the nukta layer). None of their
text or code is part of this package. The pages of romenagri-site/ link to
some of the same pages (the hindawiai/chintamani repository, DEVANAGA.TXT,
ucnvisci.cpp and the Wikipedia article on ISCII) and load nothing from any
other site: no script, no style sheet, no font.

